@startuml request-flow-offline-fallback
title Offline fallback (conf_data_dated) — the date is the staleness signal
participant App
participant "MawaqitClient" as C
participant "pages cache" as PC
participant "mawaqit.net (down)" as S
participant "snapshot dir" as D

App -> C : conf_data_dated(slug)
C -> PC : get(slug)
alt memory hit
  PC --> App : (conf, None)
else miss
  C -> S : GET /en/{slug}
  S --> C : ✗ connection refused / timeout
  alt snapshot exists
    C -> D : load(slug) — total contract
    D --> C : Some(fetched_at, conf)
    C --> App : (conf, Some(fetched_at))
  else no snapshot
    C --> App : Err(original network error)
  end
end
note over App
  Key asymmetry: a successful fetch reports None; a failed fetch reports
  Some(date) — the "how stale is this" signal, never silently enforced
  as a TTL (specs/offline-snapshots.md).
end note
@enduml
